{"name":"Paparazzi","hex":"#5a4a64","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"paparazzi","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of paparazzo"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of paparazzo.","Paparazzi taken as a group."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paparazzi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paparazzi","blocks":[{"text":"Paparazzi are independent photographers who take pictures of high-profile people, such as actors, musicians, athletes, politicians, and other celebrities who go about their daily life routines. Paparazzi are often known for their relentless pursuit of celebrities, often using telephoto lenses and electronic flashes, or even following them in vehicles to capture personal, unflattering, or private moments. The photographs taken by paparazzi are commonly sold to tabloids, gossip magazines, and websites, where they are published to attract attention and increase sales. This type of invasive photography is often controversial because it can violate the privacy of the subjects involved."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Paparazzi_La_Dolce_Vita.jpg/330px-Paparazzi_La_Dolce_Vita.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paparazzi","wikidata":"Q156624"},{"title":"Paparazzi (Lady Gaga song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Paparazzi\" is a song by American singer Lady Gaga from her debut studio album, The Fame (2008). It was released by Interscope Records as the fifth and final single from the album. Gaga wrote and co-produced the song with Rob Fusari. The song portrays Gaga's struggles in her quest for fame, as well as balancing success and love. Musically, it is an uptempo techno-pop and dance-pop ballad whose lyrics describe a stalker following somebody to grab attention and fame."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f1/Paparazzi_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paparazzi_(Lady_Gaga_song)","wikidata":"Q1025916"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Bratislava_Bronze_Paparazzo.jpg/500px-Bratislava_Bronze_Paparazzo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Bratislava_Bronze_Paparazzo.jpg/1280px-Bratislava_Bronze_Paparazzo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Bratislava_Bronze_Paparazzo.jpg/500px-Bratislava_Bronze_Paparazzo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Statue of a paparazzo by sculptor Radko Mačuha in Bratislava, Slovakia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABratislava_Bronze_Paparazzo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Barillari_rino%2C_Mickey_Hargitay%2C_vatussa_vitta%2C_Via_veneto.jpg/500px-Barillari_rino%2C_Mickey_Hargitay%2C_vatussa_vitta%2C_Via_veneto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Barillari_rino%2C_Mickey_Hargitay%2C_vatussa_vitta%2C_Via_veneto.jpg/1280px-Barillari_rino%2C_Mickey_Hargitay%2C_vatussa_vitta%2C_Via_veneto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Barillari_rino%2C_Mickey_Hargitay%2C_vatussa_vitta%2C_Via_veneto.jpg/500px-Barillari_rino%2C_Mickey_Hargitay%2C_vatussa_vitta%2C_Via_veneto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mickey Hargitay assaults the \"King of Paparazzi\" Rino Barillari while a woman hits him with her purse on Via Veneto in Rome, 1963.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarillari_rino%2C_Mickey_Hargitay%2C_vatussa_vitta%2C_Via_veneto.jpg"},{